      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Room-temperature χT = 42.55 cm3 K mol−1 (Hdc = 1000 Oe). χT decreases to 39.95 cm3 K mol−1 at 26 K then rises, consistent with Dy anisotropy/depopulation plus intramolecular ferromagnetic interactions. Field-induced slow magnetic relaxation: weak χ″ peak at 1399 Hz under zero dc field due to QTM; under 1000 Oe, χ″ peaks at 2.5–1399 Hz give Ueff/k = 100.4(3.9) K and τ0 = 1.2(0.4)×10−8 s (Arrhenius). Orbach+Raman fit gives Ueff/k = 126.5 K, n = 2.82, C = 1.13 s−1 K−2.82, τ0 = 1.22×10−9 s. Cole–Cole at 4–10 K indicates a single relaxation process (α = 0.14–0.20).",
